            <title>[MAHOUT-1572] blockify() to detect (naively) the data sparsity in the loaded data </title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/MAHOUT-1572</link>
                <project id="12310751" key="MAHOUT">Mahout</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;per &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ssc&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ssc&quot;&gt;ssc&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;br/&gt;
.bq a dense matrix is converted into a SparseRowMatrix with dense row vectors by blockify(), after serialization this becomes a dense matrix in sparse format (triggering OOMs)! &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;i guess we can look at first row vector and go on to either DenseMatrix or SparseRowMatrix&lt;/p&gt;</description>
